Not quite directly relevant to this, but also regarding hyphens:=C2=A0 I=20
recall long LONG ago, when I was making a lujvo of vofli+litru, (to=20
express just "flying along"; it looks like vofli alone would have worked=20
okay, but it may have had a different place structure then, or maybe I=20
just didn't realize it.=C2=A0 Not the point), with the rafsi -voi- plus=20
-li'u-, obviously I need a consonant hyphen to get the required=20
consonant cluster, but the rules stipulated that it *had* to be -r-,=20
thus, voirli'u. which at least to my articulatory organs felt quite=20
awkward.=C2=A0 It winds up being closer to 4 syllables than 3; the -r-=20
becomes vocalic, or nearly so.=C2=A0 Not so if I had been allowed to say=20
*voinli'u.=C2=A0 Is there a reason to forbid giving the speaker a choice=20
regarding the consonant-hyphen, given that there are only two(?) allowed=20
anyway?

~mark

